# Component Template

Use this template when creating new components:

```jsx
import resumeData from '../data/resume-data.json'

function ComponentName() {
  // Destructure data from resume JSON
  const { dataSection } = resumeData
  
  return (
    <section className="section component-name">
      <div className="container">
        <h2 className="section-title">Section Title</h2>
        
        <div className="component-content">
          {/* Main content here */}
          {dataSection.map((item, index) => (
            <div key={index} className="component-item">
              {/* Item content */}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )
}

export default ComponentName
```

## Styling Template

Add corresponding styles in `App.css`:

```css
/* Component Section */
.component-name {
  background-color: var(--bg-primary); /* or var(--bg-secondary) */
}

.component-content {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
  gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  max-width: 1000px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.component-item {
  background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
  padding: var(--spacing-lg);
  border-radius: 0.75rem;
  border: 2px solid var(--border-color);
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
}

.component-item:hover {
  transform: translateY(-4px);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  border-color: var(--accent-primary);
}

/* Responsive */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .component-content {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
```

## Integration Steps

1. Create component file in `src/components/`
2. Import in `src/App.jsx`
3. Add to `<main>` section
4. Add styles in `src/App.css`
5. Test in both light and dark modes
6. Verify mobile responsiveness
